9	Friday night market	\N	/api/media/friday-night-market.m4a	Guide: Welcome to the Friday night market. The market opens at six and the last food stall closes at eleven. Entry is free, but the cookery demonstration at eight costs five pounds and must be booked at the information tent.\nThe north row is for hot food. The busiest stall is the noodle stall, which usually sells out by nine thirty. If you want a quieter meal, the soup stall at the far end has seats.\nOn the south row you will find clothes and handmade soap. Please do not bring dogs into the south row, because of the food samples. Bicycles can be left at the green rack beside the station entrance.\nIf it rains, the music stage moves inside the old post office. Toilets are behind the clock tower. Lost children should be taken to the information tent, where a member of staff called Priya is on duty all evening.	B2	120	21	2026-10-13 14:38:15.026664+00	2026-10-13 14:38:15.026664+00	2	5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
10	Choosing a research method	\N	/api/media/choosing-a-research-method.m4a	Tutor: You both want to study how students choose their lunch. Have you decided on a method?\nLena: I prefer a questionnaire. We can collect answers from two hundred students in one week, and the canteen manager will email the link.\nOmar: The numbers would be tidy, but people rush those forms. I want to sit in the canteen for three lunchtimes and write down what they actually pick.\nLena: Observation will not tell us why they choose. A short interview, maybe fifteen people, would explain the reasons.\nTutor: You do not have time for all three. The department deadline is the twelfth of May. I suggest the questionnaire for the main result, and ten interviews to explain the surprises. Leave the observation for a later project.\nOmar: Can we record the interviews?\nTutor: Yes, if each student signs a consent form. Store the files on the university drive, not on a personal laptop.	C1	120	22	2026-10-13 14:38:15.032611+00	2026-10-13 14:38:15.032611+00	3	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
11	Why cities plant trees	\N	/api/media/why-cities-plant-trees.m4a	Lecturer: Cities plant trees for reasons that go well beyond appearance. A mature street tree can cut the temperature of the pavement beneath it by several degrees, which matters in heat waves. The leaves also catch fine dust. Studies in several European cities found lower particulate levels on tree-lined roads than on bare ones of the same width, though the difference is small on very windy days.\nRoots are a more awkward gift. They hold soil on slopes and take up storm water, so streets flood less. They also lift pavements and enter old drains. That is why new planting schemes now use underground crates, which guide the roots away from the pipes.\nSpecies choice decides whether the tree is still there in thirty years. Plane trees tolerate pollution and pruning, which is why so many avenues use them. They are a poor choice beside hospitals, because their fine hairs irritate some patients. Fruit trees feed birds, but fallen fruit makes pavements slippery, so councils usually keep them inside parks.\nThe expensive mistake is planting and then forgetting. A young tree needs water for the first three summers. After that, the main job is inspection, not daily care. Cities that budget only for the planting day lose a large share of the trees before they are big enough to shade anyone.	C1	150	23	2026-10-13 14:38:15.041597+00	2026-10-13 14:38:15.041597+00	4	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
12	A bag left on the train	\N	/api/media/a-bag-left-on-the-train.m4a	Clerk: Good afternoon, station office. How can I help you?\nCaller: Hello. I think I left my bag on the 3.15 train from Eastvale.\nClerk: Can I take your name?\nCaller: Helen Brooks. That's B-R-O-O-K-S.\nClerk: Thank you. What does the bag look like?\nCaller: It is a blue backpack. There is a grey wallet inside and a library card.\nClerk: Where did you get off?\nCaller: At Central Station, on platform 2.\nClerk: We have a blue backpack from that train. You can collect it tomorrow after 9 a.m. Please bring photo ID. There is a fee of 5 pounds.	B1	90	30	2026-10-13 15:43:01.185353+00	2026-10-13 15:43:01.185353+00	1	4	5.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
