14	Choosing an evening class	\N	/api/media/choosing-an-evening-class.m4a	Tutor: You both want an evening class. Have you chosen one?\nNina: I like the photography class on Wednesday. It starts at 6.30 and runs for eight weeks. The camera is provided.\nSam: Wednesday is my late shift. The cooking class is on Thursday, and it costs 90 pounds, which is less than photography.\nNina: Cooking finishes at 9, and the last bus on my route is at 8.45. I would have to take a taxi.\nTutor: There is also a writing class on Tuesday. It is free for library members, and it ends at 8. You only need a notebook.\nSam: Tuesday works for me. Nina, if the bus is the problem, Tuesday is safer than Thursday.\nNina: All right. Let's take the writing class. I already have a library card.	B2	100	32	2026-10-13 15:43:01.200968+00	2026-10-13 15:43:01.200968+00	3	5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
15	The community garden	\N	/api/media/the-community-garden.m4a	Speaker: The community garden behind the health centre opened in March. Twenty families share sixteen beds. Each family pays 15 pounds a year, which covers seeds and tools. Water comes from a tank on the roof, so we ask people not to leave hoses running.\nWork sessions are on Saturday morning, from 8 to 11. If you cannot come, tell the coordinator, Priya, by Friday. Tools stay in the green shed. The code for the lock is on your membership card. Please lock the shed even if you think someone else is still inside.\nWe grow vegetables, not flowers. In the first season the most successful crops were beans and lettuce. Tomatoes needed more sun than this site gets. Produce is shared among the families who worked that month. Nothing is sold. Visitors are welcome on the first Sunday of the month, but they should stay on the path.	B2	120	33	2026-10-13 15:43:01.210576+00	2026-10-13 15:43:01.210576+00	4	5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
