22	Plans for the riverside park	\N	/api/media/plans-for-the-riverside-park.m4a	Lan: The council wants ideas before they rebuild the riverside park. I read the leaflet. They will keep the playground, and they have already rejected a car park.\nMinh: Good. Parents asked for two things more than anything else: a fence around the playground, and lights along the path. A cafe would be nice, but it was near the bottom of the list. Nobody supported a stage for concerts.\nLan: For the path itself, the leaflet offers wood chips or smooth stone. Wood chips get slippery, so I would choose stone, and I would add benches every fifty metres.\nMinh: Agreed. And booking the picnic lawn should stay free for schools on weekday mornings. Companies can pay to use it after three. Weekends should remain first come, first served.\nLan: Then our two recommendations are the fence and the path lights. I will send that today.	B1	75	46	2026-10-14 02:35:54.735947+00	2026-10-14 02:35:54.735947+00	3	4.5	6	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
