25	Stalls for the school fair	\N	/api/media/stalls-for-the-school-fair.m4a	Mai: The school fair needs two stalls from our class. The list has five ideas.\nNam: A cake stall takes too long to bake. A book stall is fine, and so is a plant stall. The game stall needs prizes we do not have. The photo stall needs a camera from the office, and the office said no.\nMai: So we take the book stall and the plant stall.\nNam: Yes. Now the times. Friday at four is the football match, so the hall is full. Saturday morning is free, and Saturday afternoon is free too. Sunday is the teachers' meeting, so the hall is closed.\nMai: Then we run the stalls on Saturday morning and Saturday afternoon.	B1	70	49	2026-10-14 03:24:54.834444+00	2026-10-14 03:24:54.834444+00	3	4.5	6	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
26	Five trees on the high street	\N	/api/media/five-trees-on-the-high-street.m4a	Lecturer: The council plants five kinds of tree on the high street, and each kind has one job.\nThe oak is chosen because its roots hold the river bank. It grows slowly, so the council does not use it for shade.\nThe birch stands along the school path. Its pale bark is easy for children to see after dark.\nThe maple is placed in the square for shade in July. The leaves turn red, but colour is not the reason for planting it.\nThe willow grows beside the pond because it takes up extra water after heavy rain.\nThe pine is used next to the bus station. It stays green in winter and blocks the wind.	B2	80	50	2026-10-14 03:35:08.62723+00	2026-10-14 03:35:08.62723+00	4	5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
