33	Choosing a supervisor	\N	/api/media/choosing-a-supervisor.m4a	Lan: We need a supervisor before Friday. I read the staff notes.\nMinh: Dr Patel writes long comments on every draft, but she only meets students once a month. That would be slow when we are stuck.\nLan: Professor Okonkwo is the opposite. He sees his students every Tuesday, yet his notes are only a few lines. You leave the meeting knowing the next step, and you work out the detail yourself.\nMinh: Dr Silva understands the lab equipment better than anyone. The problem is June. She is at a conference for the whole month, and that is when we run the tests.\nLan: Ms Berger offered to help. She joined the department in September and has never supervised a thesis, so I would not ask her to be the main supervisor.\nMinh: Agreed. We can ask her about the library, and we can decide between Patel and Okonkwo tomorrow.	C1	75	57	2026-10-14 04:19:36.392093+00	2026-10-14 04:19:36.392093+00	3	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
34	Reporting a leak in the flat	\N	/api/media/reporting-a-leak-in-the-flat.m4a	Caller: Hello, is that the housing office?\nOfficer: Yes. How can I help?\nCaller: There is a leak under the kitchen sink, and the light in the hall flickers. I also have a cracked window and a radiator that stays cold.\nOfficer: The engineer can fix the leak and the hall light this week. The window is booked for next month, and the radiator needs a part that has not arrived. The bathroom tap was repaired last Friday, so that one is done.\nCaller: What should I do before the visit?\nOfficer: Please be at home between two and four, and move the pots from under the sink. There is no fee on the day. You already sent a photo, so you do not need another one. Please do not leave a key with a neighbour. Someone must be in the flat.	B2	70	58	2026-10-14 04:23:05.547154+00	2026-10-14 04:23:05.547154+00	1	5.5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
35	A walk around the art gallery	\N	/api/media/a-walk-around-the-art-gallery.m4a	Guide: Welcome to the art gallery. I will label five places on the plan. You are standing at number 1, the entrance, on the south side of the building.\nOn your left, number 2 is the shop. Cards and prints are sold there.\nNumber 3, in the middle, is the cafe. It closes at four.\nOn your right, number 4 is the studio. Children paint there on Saturday.\nStraight ahead, at the north end, number 5 is the paintings. Please do not touch them.	B1	65	59	2026-10-14 04:26:22.599325+00	2026-10-14 04:26:22.599325+00	2	4	5.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
36	Plans for the class picnic	\N	/api/media/plans-for-the-class-picnic.m4a	Lan: We need food for the class picnic.\nMinh: Let's buy bread and juice. My mum will bring a cake, so we do not need one. Crisps are too salty, and we already have apples at home.\nLan: Where can we sit on Saturday?\nMinh: The park is free in the morning, and the school field is free after lunch. The river cafe wants money. The museum garden is closed, and the sports hall is for a match.	A2	65	60	2026-10-14 04:29:24.864082+00	2026-10-14 04:29:24.864082+00	3	3.5	5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
37	Four studies of city noise	\N	/api/media/four-studies-of-city-noise.m4a	Lecturer: Four studies help the council decide where to put a night bus.\nDr Ahmed recorded sleep in fifty flats. She found that traffic noise after midnight cuts deep sleep, even when people say they are used to it.\nProfessor Lind did not stand on the street. He measured noise inside bedrooms, with the windows closed, and that figure was lower than the street reading.\nDr Costa looked at trees. A row of trees along a road lowers the noise by a small amount, but it does not remove it.\nMs Okada checked the method. She warned that one week of data is too short to judge a whole year, because summer nights are quieter than winter nights.	C1	75	61	2026-10-14 04:32:17.74254+00	2026-10-14 04:32:17.74254+00	4	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
38	A call about the bike repair	\N	/api/media/a-call-about-the-bike-repair.m4a	Caller: Hello, is that the bike shop?\nMechanic: Yes. How can I help?\nCaller: My front brake is loose, the back light is broken, and the chain is dry. There is also a small hole in the front tyre, and the bell does not ring.\nMechanic: We can fix the brake and the back light today. The chain needs oil, but that is a job for tomorrow. The hole in the tyre is too small to repair, and we do not fit bells.\nCaller: What should I bring?\nMechanic: Bring the lock and the receipt. You do not need the old brake pads. Please do not bring the basket, because we take it off. And leave the helmet at home.	B1	65	62	2026-10-14 04:35:09.392599+00	2026-10-14 04:35:09.392599+00	1	4	5.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
39	A walk around the town theatre	\N	/api/media/a-walk-around-the-town-theatre.m4a	Guide: Welcome to the town theatre. I will label five places on the plan. You are standing at number 1, the entrance, on the south side of the building.\nOn your left, number 2 is the box office. Collect your tickets there before six.\nNumber 3, in the middle, is the cloakroom. Bags stay here during the show.\nOn your right, number 4 is the cafe. It opens one hour before the play.\nStraight ahead, at the north end, number 5 is the stage. Please stay behind the rope.	B2	65	63	2026-10-14 04:38:07.501997+00	2026-10-14 04:38:07.501997+00	2	5.5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
40	A call about the conference hotel	\N	/api/media/a-call-about-the-conference-hotel.m4a	Caller: Hello, I need to change a booking for the linguistics conference.\nReceptionist: The new rate covers breakfast and the airport shuttle. It does not include dinner, a late checkout, or a desk in the room.\nCaller: Which nights are still free?\nReceptionist: We are full on Thursday night and on Sunday night. Wednesday is the night you already hold. Friday and Saturday still have rooms, so you could arrive a day later and leave before Sunday.	C1	70	64	2026-10-14 04:41:10.707649+00	2026-10-14 04:41:10.707649+00	1	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
41	Helpers for the school trip	\N	/api/media/helpers-for-the-school-trip.m4a	Lan: We need four helpers for the school trip.\nMinh: Anna brings the water. She already bought two big bottles.\nLan: Ben carries the map. He knows the path to the lake.\nMinh: Cara counts the children when we get on the bus.\nLan: Dan calls the bus company if we are late. Eva wanted to take photos, but we do not need a photographer. Tom will stay at school.	A2	60	65	2026-10-14 04:47:41.842437+00	2026-10-14 04:47:41.842437+00	3	3.5	5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
42	New rules for the river path	\N	/api/media/new-rules-for-the-river-path.m4a	Lecturer: The council is changing the river path for two reasons. The path floods after heavy rain, and the lights failed twice last winter. The change is not a response to the new cafe, and cyclists did not ask for it. The ferry timetable is also unchanged.\nTwo things will stay the same. The path remains free, and dogs can still use it on a lead. It will not stay open all night. The council will not add a cafe on the path, and it will not charge a fee.	B2	70	66	2026-10-14 05:01:58.95091+00	2026-10-14 05:01:58.95091+00	4	5.5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
45	Who is working at the sports centre	\N	/api/media/who-is-working-at-the-sports-centre.m4a	Caller: Hello, is that the sports centre?\nReceptionist: Yes. How can I help?\nCaller: Who is working today?\nReceptionist: Sam opens the pool at seven. Nina teaches the swimming class at nine. Omar sells tickets at the desk. Lily locks the doors at eight. Pat cleans the cafe, but that is a different job. Jo is off today.	A2	60	69	2026-10-14 05:22:15.106019+00	2026-10-14 05:22:15.106019+00	1	3.5	5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
46	Choosing a fieldwork site	\N	/api/media/choosing-a-fieldwork-site.m4a	Lan: We should pick the river site, not the hill.\nMinh: Agreed. The river is close to the bus, and the council already has last year's data. The hill is quieter, but that is not why we are choosing the river. The lab is not on the site, and the tutor did not recommend the hill.\nLan: What do we take?\nMinh: A permit, and waterproof notebooks. We do not need a drone. The tutor brings his own lunch. The old map is out of date, so leave it.	B2	70	70	2026-10-14 05:30:09.037969+00	2026-10-14 05:30:09.037969+00	3	5.5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
47	A visit to the city farm	\N	/api/media/a-visit-to-the-city-farm.m4a	Guide: Welcome to the city farm. Children can feed the goats and the rabbits. Please do not feed the horses. They are too big. The farmer feeds the hens, and the sheep are in the far field.\nTwo things are free. The tractor ride is free on Saturday, and you can take a map at the gate. The cafe is not free. Pony rides cost three pounds, and the shop sells postcards.	A2	65	71	2026-10-14 05:37:18.416325+00	2026-10-14 05:37:18.416325+00	2	3.5	5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
48	Who does what for the concert	\N	/api/media/who-does-what-for-the-concert.m4a	Lan: We need four people for the concert.\nMinh: Mai prints the tickets. She has the list of names.\nLan: Leo checks the sound before seven. He knows the speakers.\nMinh: Noor welcomes the parents at the door.\nLan: Chris locks the hall at the end. Pia wanted to sell drinks, but the cafe does that. Sam is away this week.	B1	60	72	2026-10-14 05:43:38.383857+00	2026-10-14 05:43:38.383857+00	3	4	5.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
49	Rules for the evening archive	\N	/api/media/rules-for-the-evening-archive.m4a	Guide: Welcome to the evening archive. Visitors may enter two rooms. The reading room is open until nine, and the catalogue room is open for the card index. The store stays locked. The seminar room is for staff tonight, and the roof store is closed for repairs.\nYou must leave two things at the desk. Leave your bag, and leave your phone. You may keep a pencil. Keep your reader's card with you, because the door checks it. Coats can stay with you.	C1	70	73	2026-10-14 06:27:18.471577+00	2026-10-14 06:27:18.471577+00	2	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
50	A talk about the school garden	\N	/api/media/a-talk-about-the-school-garden.m4a	Teacher: Hello. This is a short talk about the school garden. The garden opened in May. The children grow beans. They do not grow tomatoes. Tomatoes come from the market. Flowers are only in the park.\nThe class works in the garden on Friday afternoon. Monday is sports day, so they do not go then. Saturday is for families.\nThe river is too far. The water comes from a blue tank beside the shed. Do not use the kitchen tap. That tap is for cooking.\nThe children do not eat the beans in class. They sell them at the school fair. They do not give them to the park. The money buys new tools.	A2	70	74	2026-10-14 06:33:39.028158+00	2026-10-14 06:33:39.028158+00	4	3.5	5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
51	A call about the clinic rota	\N	/api/media/a-call-about-the-clinic-rota.m4a	Caller: Hello. I am checking the clinic rota for Thursday.\nReceptionist: Dr Khan sees the morning patients. Ms Ortiz runs the vaccine room from ten. Mr Blake answers the phone after lunch. Dr Sen reads the test results in the lab.\nCaller: Does Dr Sen answer the phone as well?\nReceptionist: No. She stays in the lab. And Mr Blake does not see patients. The evening clinic is closed on Thursday.	B2	70	75	2026-10-14 07:18:23.164834+00	2026-10-14 07:18:23.164834+00	1	5.5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
52	A call about the thesis defence	\N	/api/media/a-call-about-the-thesis-defence.m4a	Caller: Hello. I am calling about my thesis defence.\nReceptionist: It is on Thursday, in the seminar room. Wednesday is the faculty meeting, so that day is closed.\nCaller: Which floor is the room on?\nReceptionist: The third floor. The ground floor is only the waiting room.\nCaller: And the time?\nReceptionist: It starts at two. The ten o'clock slot is the library tour, not your defence.\nCaller: Should I bring a projector?\nReceptionist: No. The slides are already on the room computer. Please bring two printed copies of the thesis. The examiners sit at the front table. You stand at the lectern. Guests sit at the back.	C1	70	76	2026-10-14 08:00:54.995325+00	2026-10-14 08:00:54.995325+00	1	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
53	Who planned the school show	\N	/api/media/who-planned-the-school-show.m4a	Teacher: This short talk is about the people who planned the school show. Mia chooses the songs. She does not sell tickets. Tom sells the tickets at the door. Sara paints the posters. Jack checks the lights before the show. Nina wanted to sing, but the choir is already full. Ben is away this week.	B1	70	77	2026-10-14 08:08:58.454391+00	2026-10-14 08:08:58.454391+00	4	4	5.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
54	A call about a flat viewing	\N	/api/media/a-call-about-a-flat-viewing.m4a	Agent: Good afternoon. How can I help?\nCaller: I would like to view the flat. My surname is Brooks.\nAgent: Thank you, Ms Brooks. Thursday is full. The next viewing is on Friday.\nCaller: What time on Friday?\nAgent: Not at five. The five o'clock slot has gone. Yours is at six.\nCaller: Is the flat on Hill Street?\nAgent: No. It is on River Street. I will meet you there. My name is Nina. The owner will not be at home.	B2	70	78	2026-10-14 08:08:58.468972+00	2026-10-14 08:08:58.468972+00	1	5.5	6.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
55	A call about the conference badge	\N	/api/media/a-call-about-the-conference-badge.m4a	Clerk: Conference office. How can I help?\nCaller: I need a badge for Friday. My surname is Hale.\nClerk: Thank you, Dr Hale. Your session is in room fourteen, not room forty.\nCaller: Does the fee include dinner?\nClerk: No. Dinner is extra. Lunch is included.\nCaller: Where do I collect the badge?\nClerk: At the desk in the lobby. The hall does not issue badges.	C1	70	79	2026-10-14 08:08:58.479197+00	2026-10-14 08:08:58.479197+00	1	6	7.5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
56	Plans for the class party	\N	/api/media/plans-for-the-class-party.m4a	Anna: Let's have the class party on Friday.\nBen: Friday is the football match. Saturday is better.\nAnna: Saturday morning?\nBen: No. Saturday afternoon. The morning is the swimming class.\nAnna: Where shall we have it?\nBen: Not in the classroom. The classroom is too small. Let's use the school hall.\nAnna: What food shall we buy?\nBen: Cake. Not pizza. Pizza is too expensive. And juice, not cola.	A2	70	80	2026-10-14 08:16:14.604155+00	2026-10-14 08:16:14.604155+00	3	3.5	5	EDU APP English (giọng đọc máy)	original
