30	Street trees on Market Road	A\nMarket Road used to be a wide street of shops with almost no shade. In summer the pavement was too hot to stand on at noon, and several shopkeepers asked the council for trees.\n\nB\nThe council planted twenty young trees in 2021. It chose species that stay narrow, so the branches would not hide the shop signs. Each tree sits in a square of soil cut into the pavement.\n\nC\nThe first summer was difficult. Two trees died because the soil dried out, and a van broke a third when it parked on the pavement. The council replaced those three and fitted a low rail around every square.\n\nD\nShopkeepers now open their doors earlier in hot weather, and a survey in 2024 found that most customers noticed the street was cooler. The survey did not measure sales, so nobody can say the trees increased trade.\n\nE\nThe council will plant ten more trees next year, but only where the pavement is wide enough for a wheelchair to pass. It will not remove parking spaces to make room.	B2	EDU APP English	12	37	2026-10-14 01:59:45.82431+00	2026-10-14 01:59:45.82431+00	ACADEMIC	Environment	5	6.5	original
