37	Leaf blowers on city streets	Leaf blowers have become a regular part of city maintenance, and the present free-for-all is a mistake. Crews use the machines at all hours, including Sunday mornings, when the noise carries straight into bedrooms.\nI do not accept the claim that electric models settle the matter. They are quieter than petrol ones, and they avoid the fumes, but they are not silent. A neighbour can still be woken by one.\nA total ban appeals to some campaigners. That would be the wrong remedy. Crews would simply move the same work to the weekend, when more residents are at home. The better rule is to allow the machines on weekday mornings only, and to stop them by noon.\nCouncils that have tried this rule report fewer complaints. Whether an electric model costs less to buy than a petrol one is a question for the purchasing office. It is not part of the argument here.	C1	EDU APP English	8	50	2026-10-14 04:04:52.639686+00	2026-10-14 04:04:52.639686+00	ACADEMIC	Town planning	6	7.5	original
